## Broadband Initiative

Mohawk Networks is currently building out a fiber network throughout the St. Regis Mohawk tribal lands. As part of this initiative, Mohawk Networks received a $5 million dollar grant from the Tribal Broadband Connectivity Program (TBCP). Mohawk Networks also applied for a New York State ConnectALL grant to expand broadband service, including more areas of the St. Regis Mohawk tribal lands. They currently service approximately 1,500 homes and businesses, and plan to expand by building more fiber to the home (FTTH) service as part of this initiative. Mohawk Networks also has a mesh network utilizing existing infrastructure. They currently plan to expand fiber to more than 900 locations.

---

## Partners & Vendors

Mohawk Networks has a network of trusted partners and vendors who support their broadband infrastructure.

---

## Centillion

Centillion is a fiber network engineering and construction management firm. Centillion serves as the fiber engineering firm for Mohawk Networks, providing network design, OSP (outside plant) engineering, and construction management services.

---

## ISN - Internet Services of New York

ISN serves as the data management company for Mohawk Networks, handling data center management, transit/bandwidth, and IP management.

